+### PINN : required data
+The PINN scripts (`train_PINN.py`, `test_PINN.py`) cannot run from a fresh clone:
+- `./dataset/KSTAR_rl_GS_solver.csv` : table of KSTAR EFIT reconstructions with 0D columns
+  `\ipmhd, \q95, \betap, \li`, PF-coil currents `\PCPF1U ... \PCPF7U` and a `path` column pointing to
+  one `.npz` file per equilibrium (keys `psi`, `R`, `Z`, 65 x 65 grid). **Not included** (`dataset/` is git-ignored).
+- `./src/GSsolver/toy_dataset/g028911_004060.npz` (+ g-file `g028911.004060`) : one KSTAR sample equilibrium used
+  for the grid and plots. **Not included any more** (deleted in commit `c0b741f`); it can be recovered from history :
+  `mkdir -p src/GSsolver/toy_dataset && git show e39e56a:src/GSsolver/toy_dataset/g028911_004060.npz > src/GSsolver/toy_dataset/g028911_004060.npz`
+- trained weights `./weights/PINN_best.pt` : **not included** (deleted in commit `7be12f6`); `train_PINN.py` writes them to `./weights/`.
+- GPU : the original training used CUDA GPUs (`--gpu_num`). The code now falls back to CPU when CUDA is not available,
+  so all PINN modules import on CPU-only machines, but full training on CPU is expected to be very slow (not tested).
+Without these files the scripts stop with a `FileNotFoundError` that points to this section.
+
+## Known limitations / fixes 2026-09-29
+Full list of changes (file, before -> after, why): [`CHANGES-2026-09-29.md`](CHANGES-2026-09-29.md).
+- **Fixed** : README commands failed (`ModuleNotFoundError: src.grad_shafranov`, `SyntaxError` in
+  `src/numerical/grad_shafranov.py`, undefined `GSMatrix`, missing `_computes` module, missing `environment.yaml`,
+  removed SciPy APIs `interp2d` / `scipy.linalg.decomp_qr`, CUDA calls that crash on CPU-only machines).
+- **Fixed** : Green's function of a circular filament used `ellipk(k)` / `ellipe(k)` although SciPy expects the
+  parameter m = k^2. The flux was overestimated by +9 % right next to the filament, +42 % at k^2 = 0.95
+  (3.355e-7 instead of 2.355e-7 Wb/rad/A), x8 at k^2 = 0.5 and by orders of magnitude for distant points (k^2 -> 0).
+  Now verified against direct Biot-Savart quadrature to < 1e-6 (`tests/test_green.py`). This also affects the
+  PINN copy in `src/GSsolver/GradShafranov.py`; **results / figures produced by the PINN before this fix
+  (`result/PINN_*.png`) were computed with the wrong Green's function and were not regenerated.**
+- **Fixed** : free-boundary solver : psi on **all four** edges from the Green's function of plasma + coils (was: a
+  single averaged value from two edges), plasma mask psi_N < 1 connected to the axis (was: current everywhere),
+  Ip constraint, sparse direct solve, R/Z axes in `plotGrid` (were swapped). `result/Free-Boundary-Equilibrium.png`
+  is the old (incorrect) figure; the new one is `result/Free-Boundary-Equilibrium-fixed.png`.
+- **Changed defaults** of `test_free_boundary.py` : the old single 1 A coil at (1.5, 0.25) m lay *inside* the grid
+  (singular flux, now rejected with a `ValueError`) and there was no plasma-current constraint. New defaults: see above.
+- **Limitation** : the last closed flux surface is limited by the rectangular computational box (psi_b = extremum of
+  psi on the edge). There is no X-point search, no real limiter/wall contour and no coil-current feedback, so
+  diverted shapes cannot be computed and the plasma position depends on the chosen coil currents. Picard iteration
+  without position feedback is radially/vertically unstable for many coil sets (the plasma then drifts to the wall;
+  check the printed axis position and the figure).
+- **Limitation** : only the J_phi profile `lamda (beta_0 R/R0 + (1-beta_0) R0/R)(1 - psi_N^m)^n` with fixed `beta_0`;
+  no beta_p constraint in the free-boundary example.
+- **Limitation** : the legacy fixed-boundary path (`test_boundary.py`, `src/numerical/tokamak.py`, class `GSsolver`,
+  `profiles.py`, `boundary.py`) now imports, but its algorithm still fails at run time (axis search finds no
+  magnetic axis, `ValueError` in `boundary.py`) and uses dense O(N^4) loops. It was not repaired.
+- **Not tested** : PINN training/evaluation (no data, no GPU). Only imports on CPU and the Green's function were checked.
 
